wv: -std=gnu89 in place of -ansi.

configure gives GCC "-ansi" (ANSI_CFLAGS, added to every compile). QNX's qcc
driver rejects that option ("cc: -ansi no longer supported"), so nothing
compiled. -std=gnu89 is the language level -ansi selected for this 1990s C
code, with the GNU extensions the system headers expect. configure is
changed along with configure.ac, so the tarball builds without autoreconf.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

diff -ru a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure	2010-10-10 06:27:13.000000000 +0900
+++ b/configure	2026-11-25 17:30:02.347900931 +0900
@@ -4117,7 +4117,7 @@
 
 
 if test "x$GCC" = "xyes"; then
-	ANSI_CFLAGS="-ansi"
+	ANSI_CFLAGS="-std=gnu89"
 else
 	ANSI_CFLAGS=""
 fi
diff -ru a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac	2010-10-10 06:26:22.000000000 +0900
+++ b/configure.ac	2026-11-25 17:30:02.346210125 +0900
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 
 AC_PROG_CC
 if test "x$GCC" = "xyes"; then
-	ANSI_CFLAGS="-ansi"
+	ANSI_CFLAGS="-std=gnu89"
 else
 	ANSI_CFLAGS=""
 fi
